    "amendment_reason": "the prior v2 association preserved within-episode identities but not one graph across episodes; a source-only cross-action probe then showed that rigid one-to-one registration fails under grasp occlusion, so the locked method keeps one graph while completing its state from partial observations; the official Deform360 paper also defines multi-episode evaluation as prediction on an entirely unseen interaction, so the observation boundary is tightened prospectively from a six-frame response prefix to frame zero only; a source-action-only audit over all 30 source episodes showed that the fixed raw interval captured only 24.94 percent of the best equal-length controller displacement and 33.45 percent of the best path; the first displacement-maximizing amendment was then falsified on source episode 002-rope-silk/0 because 83.07 mm mean controller displacement coincided with only 0.597 mm mean object displacement and the video showed open-gripper approach rather than manipulation; before any calibration dynamics, target action, target initial frame, or target outcome was read, the selector was therefore amended to maximize gripper path weighted by robust closure confidence from the released future action aperture",
